bioqore-synthetic-data-project (Bioqore), setpoint snapping
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: github.com/Bioqore/bioqore-synthetic-data-project (commit 1cc393e),
generators/base.py (snap_discrete_setpoints), by Srihan Vege and James Hassett
for Bioqore.

Idea credit; re-implemented, no code copied. The idea taken is that a lab
setpoint is not continuous: a generated value is snapped to a level the lab can
actually make. Kalos applies it to proposed recipes in kalos/core/resolution.py
(round each input to its declared step, its declared levels or 4 significant
figures, toward the feasible side of the bounds and linear constraints). The
repository has no license file; no source line from it is included here.
